Session summary — wrapping at the relay boundary:

**Recovered from the host reset and got the cluster back.** The manual reset meant the @reboot recovery hook never ran; the missing piece was that test1–test16 can't even `virsh start` until the host is iSCSI-logged-in to all 16 per-node targets (their disks are by-path passthroughs). I logged in all 16, fixed `clyde_boot_recover.sh` to do all 17 logins on future boots, recreated `/tmp/.mxfs_pass`, and `cluster_reset_n.sh 16` came up clean on build `DE7F1BDA`. `zero_silent_loss` then passed 3/3 — confirming last session's failure was the SCST wedge, not mxfs. (Also: yes, the reset script is fully parallel across nodes, and I delivered the SCST-wedge prompt for Opus, which is now working on disk2 — properly isolated from my disk1.)

**Completed the ship probe-gating sweep.** A passing run was still emitting ~36k `mxfs: P*` printk lines cluster-wide plus `dump_stack()` Call Traces (a `dmesg_clean` failure waiting to happen). I hand-gated the hot first batch, then four parallel agents gated the remaining ~46 sites behind `mxfs.dirwr || mxfs.instr` (dlm/ via dual-build-safe helpers). I diff-reviewed every hunk against `.backup` copies — all gates are print-only, lock-path semantics untouched. Build `4450524B` deployed to all 16 nodes.

**The gated build exposed two real latent races — `zero_silent_loss` now FAILS.** Run 1: one created-then-lost dirent (the sess15 class). Run 2: an EUCLEAN corruption storm — `corrupt dinode 131 (btree extents)` at `xfs_iread_bmbt_block`, the known torn dinode-vs-bmbt family on the hot shared dir. The ~36k printks were evidently serializing the dir hot paths enough to mask these. They are real mxfs bugs that must be fixed at full speed — not papered over by re-adding prints.

**Next session:** reproduce under `mxfs.dirwr=1` (the purpose-built low-rate detector set for exactly this family), harvest the ino-131 dinode/bmbt timeline, root-fix the torn write, then re-pass `zero_silent_loss` on the silent build and run `verify_ship.sh` end-to-end. Everything is captured in memory (`sess38-probe-gating-exposed-races`). Criteria not met — marker not written.

